Result: the TurboFilter masks user parameter before formatting. Records are reconstructed with masked components; POJOs are masked in place; nested lists and maps are traversed; only configured log levels are processed.

Notes and limitations
Records are reconstructed so immutability is preserved. If a record constructor is inaccessible or fails, the original record is left unchanged as a safe fallback.

Unmodifiable containers are not replaced; objects they reference are masked in place when possible. If a container prevents mutation of its elements, nested mutable objects are still processed.

Performance: deep graphs and heavy reflection are costly. Restrict masking to appropriate log levels and avoid masking on extremely hot paths.

Thread safety: the masker mutates objects in place for POJOs; if objects are shared concurrently, consider cloning strategies or restricting masking to non‑concurrent contexts.

Extensibility: add named strategies (LAST4, FIRST3) by implementing MaskingStrategy and selecting them via annotation metadata or configuration.

